district | v7 | 40.5 | degrees-C-WBGT | current |\n| CLI-065 | river-district | v8 | 39.3 | degrees-C-WBGT | current |\n| CLI-066 | central-core | v8 | 41.0 | degrees-C-WBGT | current |\n| CLI-067 | hillside | v8 | 39.8 | degrees-C-WBGT | current |\n| CLI-068 | north-district | v8 | 41.5 | degrees-C-WBGT | current |\n| CLI-069 | river-district | v8 | 40.3 | degrees-C-WBGT | superseded |\n| CLI-070 | central-core | v8 | 39.1 | degrees-C-WBGT | current |\n| CLI-071 | hillside | v8 | 40.8 | degrees-C-WBGT | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve observed versus activation values, windows, probability, coverage, and currentness.\nDefine falsifiers, district rollback, and evidence that retires a heat stage.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"end_line\":60,\"source_id\":\"GRID\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":60,\"source_id\":\"WATER\",\"start_line\":1}]}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:GRID:1-60+WATER:1-60\",\"object_version\":\"d1ecb3814186f1a6327e7fa1b8a7befd76b1617b06163bb6a426511c6e355be8\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-015\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":60,\"source_id\":\"GRID\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":60,\"source_id\":\"WATER\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":7344}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":60,\"source_id\":\"GRID\",\"source_path\":\"sources/GRID_COOLING_POWER.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"2149dcb753ebd817f10869d394e30f61e89ac46d6d4de2ace9bde1cb7c13299d\",\"source_size_bytes\":5546,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Cooling power, feeder limits, and backup capacity\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nInstalled cooling-service capacity is 31.0 megawatts, while current usable capacity after feeder derating is 24.5 megawatts. Installed and usable capacity must not be added or swapped.\nFeeder voltage is 12.6 kilovolts and must remain between 12.2 and 12.9 kilovolts at every critical node for three consecutive fifteen-minute windows. A system average cannot replace every-node compliance.\nBackup generation supplies 8.4 megawatts for sixteen hours at emergency cooling load, but only nine hours at full public load. The load regimes and durations remain distinct.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nSHELTER occupancy and CLINIC surge demand depend on GRID; SUPPLY controls fuel duration and WATER depends on powered pumps.\nA feeder, transformer, relay, fuel stock, or facility-load change makes earlier power evidence stale.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| GRD-000 | feeder-east | v3 | 28.0 | megawatts | superseded |\n| GRD-001 | feeder-west | v3 | 29.7 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-002 | library-hub | v3 | 28.5 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-003 | backup-plant | v3 | 30.2 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-004 | feeder-east | v3 | 29.0 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-005 | feeder-west | v3 | 30.7 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-006 | library-hub | v3 | 29.5 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-007 | backup-plant | v3 | 28.3 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-008 | feeder-east | v3 | 30.0 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-009 | feeder-west | v3 | 28.8 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-010 | library-hub | v3 | 30.5 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-011 | backup-plant | v3 | 29.3 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-012 | feeder-east | v3 | 28.1 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-013 | feeder-west | v4 | 29.8 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-014 | library-hub | v4 | 28.6 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-015 | backup-plant | v4 | 30.3 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-016 | feeder-east | v4 | 29.1 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-017 | feeder-west | v4 | 30.8 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-018 | library-hub | v4 | 29.6 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-019 | backup-plant | v4 | 28.4 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-020 | feeder-east | v4 | 30.1 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-021 | feeder-west | v4 | 28.9 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-022 | library-hub | v4 | 30.6 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-023 | backup-plant | v4 | 29.4 | megawatts | superseded |\n| GRD-024 | feeder-east | v4 | 28.2 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-025 | feeder-west | v4 | 29.9 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-026 | library-hub | v5 | 28.7 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-027 | backup-plant | v5 | 30.4 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-028 | feeder-east | v5 | 29.2 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-029 | feeder-west | v5 | 28.0 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-030 | library-hub | v5 | 29.7 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-031 | backup-plant | v5 | 28.5 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-032 | feeder-east | v5 | 30.2 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-033 | feeder-west | v5 | 29.0 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-034 | library-hub | v5 | 30.7 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-035 | backup-plant | v5 | 29.5 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-036 | feeder-east | v5 | 28.3 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-037 | feeder-west | v5 | 30.0 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-038 | library-hub | v5 | 28.8 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-039 | backup-plant | v6 | 30.5 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-040 | feeder-east | v6 | 29.3 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-041 | feeder-west | v6 | 28.1 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-042 | library-hub | v6 | 29.8 | megawatts | current |\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":60,\"source_id\":\"WATER\",\"source_path\":\"sources/WATER_HYDRATION.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"99ff010ef7c523ff6805b118fb7678a403caf6cfb047f9a7607832a51f1e4291\",\"source_size_bytes\":5054,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Potable water, pressure, and hydration logistics\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nCurrent minimum pressure is 38 psi. Public cooling sites require at least 35 psi at every served node for three consecutive ten-minute windows; one network average is insufficient.\nPotable reserve is 1.6 million liters, while forecast consumption is 0.19 million liters per hour at expanded operations. Reserve and hourly flow use different units and must not be added.\nA main repair, pump change, tank refill, disinfection event, sampling method, or candidate facility-roster change makes earlier water evidence stale.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nGRID powers pumps, SHELTER and CLINIC consume potable reserve, and SUPPLY controls tanker replenishment.\nREVIEW requires current pressure and quality evidence before closure; COUNCIL retains operating authority.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| WTR-000 | north-loop | v3 | 38.0 | psi | superseded |\n| WTR-001 | central-loop | v3 | 39.7 | psi | current |\n| WTR-002 | clinic-tank | v3 | 38.5 | psi | current |\n| WTR-003 | mobile-cache | v3 | 40.2 | psi | current |\n| WTR-004 | north-loop | v3 | 39.0 | psi | current |\n| WTR-005 | central-loop | v3 | 40.7 | psi | current |\n| WTR-006 | clinic-tank | v3 | 39.5 | psi | current |\n| WTR-007 | mobile-cache | v3 | 38.3 | psi | current |\n| WTR-008 | north-loop | v3 | 40.0 | psi | current |\n| WTR-009 | central-loop | v3 | 38.8 | psi | current |\n| WTR-010 | clinic-tank | v3 | 40.5 | psi | current |\n| WTR-011 | mobile-cache | v3 | 39.3 | psi | current |\n| WTR-012 | north-loop | v3 | 38.1 | psi | current |\n| WTR-013 | central-loop | v4 | 39.8 | psi | current |\n| WTR-014 | clinic-tank | v4 | 38.6 | psi | current |\n| WTR-015 | mobile-cache | v4 | 40.3 | psi | current |\n| WTR-016 | north-loop | v4 | 39.1 | psi | current |\n| WTR-017 | central-loop | v4 | 40.8 | psi | current |\n| WTR-018 | clinic-tank | v4 | 39.6 | psi | current |\n| WTR-019 | mobile-cache | v4 | 38.4 | psi | current |\n| WTR-020 | north-loop | v4 | 40.1 | psi | current |\n| WTR-021 | central-loop | v4 | 38.9 | psi | current |\n| WTR-022 | clinic-tank | v4 | 40.6 | psi | current |\n| WTR-023 | mobile-cache | v4 | 39.4 | psi | superseded |\n| WTR-024 | north-loop | v4 | 38.2 | psi | current |\n|