hree consecutive fifteen-minute windows. A system average cannot replace every-node compliance.\nBackup generation supplies 8.4 megawatts for sixteen hours at emergency cooling load, but only nine hours at full public load. The load regimes and durations remain distinct.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nSHELTER occupancy and CLINIC surge demand depend on GRID; SUPPLY controls fuel duration and WATER depends on powered pumps.\nA feeder, transformer, relay, fuel stock, or facility-load change makes earlier power evidence stale.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| GRD-000 | feeder-east | v3 | 28.0 | megawatts | superseded |\n| GRD-001 | feeder-west | v3 | 29.7 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-002 | library-hub | v3 | 28.5 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-003 | backup-plant | v3 | 30.2 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-004 | feeder-east | v3 | 29.0 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-005 | feeder-west | v3 | 30.7 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-006 | library-hub | v3 | 29.5 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-007 | backup-plant | v3 | 28.3 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-008 | feeder-east | v3 | 30.0 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-009 | feeder-west | v3 | 28.8 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-010 | library-hub | v3 | 30.5 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-011 | backup-plant | v3 | 29.3 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-012 | feeder-east | v3 | 28.1 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-013 | feeder-west | v4 | 29.8 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-014 | library-hub | v4 | 28.6 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-015 | backup-plant | v4 | 30.3 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-016 | feeder-east | v4 | 29.1 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-017 | feeder-west | v4 | 30.8 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-018 | library-hub | v4 | 29.6 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-019 | backup-plant | v4 | 28.4 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-020 | feeder-east | v4 | 30.1 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-021 | feeder-west | v4 | 28.9 | megawatts | current |\