s alone are insufficient.\nMedian route time is 26 minutes and p95 is 44 minutes. Median and p95 serve different planning purposes and must remain distinct.\nA vehicle, route, driver roster, accessibility lift, traffic plan, or candidate facility map change makes earlier transit evidence stale.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nSHELTER arrival planning consumes TRANSIT capacity, LABOR supplies drivers, and COMMS publishes only confirmed routes.\nCLIMATE changes geographic staging and LINEAGE binds the route map to the current candidate.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| TRN-000 | route-red | v3 | 88.0 | percent-available | superseded |\n| TRN-001 | route-blue | v3 | 89.7 | percent-available | current |\n| TRN-002 | paratransit | v3 | 88.5 | percent-available | current |\n| TRN-003 | shuttle-reserve | v3 | 90.2 | percent-available | current |\n| TRN-004 | route-red | v3 | 89.0 | percent-available | current |\n| TRN-005 | route-blue | v3 | 90.7 | percent-available | current |\n| TRN-006 | paratransit | v3 | 89.5 | percent-available | current |\n| TRN-007 | shuttle-reserve | v3 | 88.3 | percent-available | current |\n| TRN-008 | route-red | v3 | 90.0 | percent-available | current |\n| TRN-009 | route-blue | v3 | 88.8 | percent-available | current |\n| TRN-010 | paratransit | v3 | 90.5 | percent-available | current |\n| TRN-011 | shuttle-reserve | v3 | 89.3 | percent-available | current |\n| TRN-012 | route-red | v3 | 88.1 | percent-available | current |\n| TRN-013 | route-blue | v4 | 89.8 | percent-available | current |\n| TRN-014 | paratransit | v4 | 88.6 | percent-available | current |\n| TRN-015 | shuttle-reserve | v4 | 90.3 | percent-available | current |\n| TRN-016 | route-red | v4 | 89.1 | percent-available | current |\n| TRN-017 | route-blue | v4 | 90.8 | percent-available | current |\n| TRN-018 | paratransit | v4 | 89.6 | percent-available | current |\n| TRN-019 | shuttle-rese