\n\nHeat guidance reached 89 percent of subscribed households; eleven percent remains delivery uncertainty, not an eleven-percent reduction in exposed residents.\nPublic-state delivery is 680 milliseconds at p95 and 1,140 milliseconds at p99. These observations are not response deadlines.\nThe call center sustains 1,300 contacts per hour for three hours against forecast demand of 1,750 per hour unless multilingual outbound notices reduce repeat calls.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nCOUNCIL determines authorized state language; CLIMATE supplies hazard scope and TRANSIT and SHELTER supply confirmed service facts.\nA channel, subscriber list, message release, translation, coverage method, or candidate operating state change makes earlier communication evidence stale.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| COM-000 | sms | v3 | 89.0 | percent-delivered | superseded |\n| COM-001 | radio | v3 | 90.7 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-002 | web | v3 | 89.5 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-003 | call-center | v3 | 91.2 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-004 | sms | v3 | 90.0 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-005 | radio | v3 | 91.7 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-006 | web | v3 | 90.5 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-007 | call-center | v3 | 89.3 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-008 | sms | v3 | 91.0 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-009 | radio | v3 | 89.8 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-010 | web | v3 | 91.5 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-011 | call-center | v3 | 90.3 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-012 | sms | v3 | 89.1 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-013 | radio | v4 | 90.8 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-014 | web | v4 | 89.6 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-015 | call-center | v4 | 91.3 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-016 | sms | v4 | 90.1 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-017 | radio | v4 |